BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mother Goose on the Loose! (Davis)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T103000
UID:a07cbd2da22497b9edbf453e3de5877b@events.yolocountylibrary.org
DESCRIPTION:Join Ms. Sue for Mother Goose on the Loose!\n\nMother Goose on
  the Loose is an award-winning early literacy program for toddlers (ages 2
 -3) and their grown-ups.  It combines music\, movement\, rhymes\, and boo
 ks to help young children develop language skills\, social and emotional s
 kills\, general knowledge about the world\, and a love of learning.\n\nEve
 ry Tuesday in the Blanchard Room of the Mary L. Stephens Davis Branch Lib
 rary.
LOCATION:Blanchard Room\, Mary L Stephens Davis Branch Library
URL:https://events.yolocountylibrary.org/event/15530977
X-SOURCE:Yolo Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sexual Violence Prevention and Education presented by Empower Yolo
  & Communicare+OLE (Spanish & English)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260728T193000
UID:d27ac7cff9ffc2f9ae1ef91ae9575cb3@events.yolocountylibrary.org
DESCRIPTION:Objectives of the Sexual Violence Prevention and Education Pro
 gram. Enhance the organizational capacity to prevent sexual violence and 
 promote health equity for priority populations.\n\n\n	Engage a network of 
 partners\, organizations\, and community members/residents.\n\n\nFocusing 
 on the following strategies:\n1) Economic stability and mobility for women
 \, gender-diverse individuals\, and families\n2) Transforming gender norms
 \n\nOverview of the Primary Prevention Promoter Program.\n\n\n	Introductio
 n to the Primary Prevention Promoters Program Foundations: What Does It Me
 an to Be a Promoter? What Is Sexual Violence?\n	Self-Reflection Part 1: Se
 lf-Reflection Can Facilitate the Development of Awareness and Empathy\n	Se
 lf-Reflection Part 2: Self-Care\n	Social Justice Approach to Violence Prev
 ention\n	Financial Empowerment Part 1: Economic Security and Navigating Go
 vernment Programs\n	Financial Empowerment Part 2 Gender Norms\n	Healthy Co
 mmunication and Relationships\n	Warning Signs\n	Trauma-Informed Skills/De-
 escalation and Leadership\n	Next Steps/Taking Action/Action Plan\n\n\nProg
 ram will be in Spanish and English\n\nParticipants must register in advanc
 e HERE \n\nBecome a part of our team. For the welfare of the community!\
 n\nFor information\, please call Maria Elena at 530.405.9243 or 530.665.53
 20\nYou can contact us by email at promotora@empoweryolo.org
LOCATION:*Children's Activity Room\, Mary L Stephens Davis Branch Library
URL:https://events.yolocountylibrary.org/event/16385000
X-SOURCE:Yolo Library
END:VEVENT
